{"name":"If a Tree Fell …","hex":"#6f5a4a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tree","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A perennial woody plant taller and larger than a shrub with a wooden trunk and, at some distance from the ground, having leaves and branches.","Any other plant (such as a large shrub or herb) that is reminiscent of the above in form and size."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To chase (an animal or person) up a tree.","To place in a tree."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tree"},{"term":"fell","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make something fall, especially a tree.","To strike down; to kill; to destroy."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A cutting-down of timber.","The stitching down of a fold of cloth; specifically, the portion of a kilt, from the waist to the seat, where the pleats are stitched down."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fell"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tree","blocks":[{"text":"In botany, a tree is a perennial plant with an elongated stem, or trunk, usually supporting branches and leaves. In some usages, the definition of a tree may be narrower, e.g., including only woody plants with secondary growth, only plants that are usable for timber, or only plants above a specified height. Wider definitions include taller palms, tree ferns, bananas, and bamboos."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Usamljeni_jasen_-_panoramio_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Usamljeni_jasen_-_panoramio_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tree"},{"title":"Fell","blocks":[{"text":"A fell is a high and barren landscape feature, such as a mountain or moor-covered hill, often mountain landscape over the tree line, etc. The term is most often employed in Fennoscandia, Iceland, the Isle of Man, parts of northern England, and Scotland."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/K%C3%A5rtejaure_from_treeline.jpg/330px-K%C3%A5rtejaure_from_treeline.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fell"},{"title":"Ellipsis","blocks":[{"text":"The ellipsis, rendered ..., also known as suspension points, dots, periods of ellipsis, or ellipsis points, or, colloquially, dot, dot, dot is a punctuation mark consisting of a series of three dots. An ellipsis can be used in many ways, such as for intentional omission of text or numbers, to imply a concept without using words, or to mark a pause in speech. Style guides differ on how to render an ellipsis both digitally and in print. In some cases, an ellipsis may have two, four or more dots, spaced dots, or some incorporation with other punctuation."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellipsis"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Larix_decidua_Aletschwald.jpg/500px-Larix_decidua_Aletschwald.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Larix_decidua_Aletschwald.jpg/1280px-Larix_decidua_Aletschwald.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Larix_decidua_Aletschwald.jpg/500px-Larix_decidua_Aletschwald.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"European larch (Larix decidua), a coniferous tree which is also deciduous[2]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALarix_decidua_Aletschwald.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Nedravazhakola.jpg/500px-Nedravazhakola.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Nedravazhakola.jpg/1280px-Nedravazhakola.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x",